e Dark ritual.<br /> Social: Charisma unknown, Manipulation 10, Appearance n/a<br /> Mental: Unknown, Wits 10 (Abyss Mysticism)<br /> Talents: Unknown<br /> Skills: Unknown<br /> Knowledges: Unknown, Occult 10 (Obtenebration)<br /> Disciplines: Dominate 10, Fortitude 3, Mytherceria 4, Obfuscate 3, Obtenebration 10, Potence 10, Presence 3<br /> Combination Disciplines: Armor of the Abyss; Bagman\u2019s Shelter; Dreamstalker; Empower Minion; Fear of the Dark; Mind Strike; Reluctant Performance Artist; Sacrifice to Nightmare; Shadow Mark; Shroud of Absence; Tenebrous Veil<br /> Abyss Mysticism Rituals: Light within Shadow, Weight of Shadows, Comforting Darkness, Feed the Darkness, Abyssal Threads, Claiming the Dark, Maw of Ahriman, Vision of Shadow, Ahriman\u2019s Wight, Commune with the Abyss<br /> Backgrounds: Allies 5 (Louhi)<br /> Virtues: Unknown<br /> Morality: Unknown<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Merits: Aura of Command, Bruiser, Call of the Sea, Controllable Night Sight, Enchanting Voice, Eyes of Shadow 4, Long-Term Planning, Natural Leader, Natural Linguist, Rep, Secret Stash 5<br /> Flaws: Cold Breeze, Clan Enmity (Lasombra), Eerie Presence, Hunted Like a Dog (Sabbat), Lord of the Night, Methuselah\u2019s Thirst, Nightmares, Touch of Frost<br /> Health Levels: OK x30<br /> Blood Pool/Max per Turn: 75/15<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>We are aware that the antes are plot-devices, but it seems lazy and of course, we understand that every game has its own reach on this topic. But we want an objective evaluation of these characters.</u></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-02-2026, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T07:32:47-07:00","id":1383955,"title":"","content":"I always think antes aren\u2019t true plot devices, they\u2019re just so powerful that only \u201cplot devices\u201d can describe them, but their maximum are still 10, after all. 10 dices, their dice pool is usually 20+, and they can also botch, then...<br /> <br /> If you follow the now-noncanon Gehenna, then the traits of original antes are all 8-10","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-26-2020, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T08:15:28-07:00","id":1383957,"title":"","content":"No stats for antes, VtM is not D&amp;D (and even D&amp;D stopped giving stats to gods, or at least Pathfinder did).<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> The &quot;argument&quot; that not giving stats to a plot device would be &quot;lazy&quot; is patently ridicolous. The work a ST does is not in putting some numbers on paper, it's about building a complex, often multilayered plot involving such characters, which is the exact opposite of &quot;lazy&quot;. And it doesn't help that those who want to stat everything are usually those players who dream about killing anything they meet in order to &quot;win&quot; at roleplaying...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 04-26-2020, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T08:31:55-07:00","id":1383959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1383957#post1383957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No stats for antes, VtM is not D&amp;D (and even D&amp;D stopped giving stats to gods, or at least Pathfinder did).<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> The &quot;argument&quot; that not giving stats to a plot device would be &quot;lazy&quot; is patently ridicolous. The work a ST does is not in putting some numbers on paper, it's about building a complex, often multilayered plot involving such characters, which is the exact opposite of &quot;lazy&quot;. And it doesn't help that those who want to stat everything are usually those players who dream about killing anything they meet in order to &quot;win&quot; at roleplaying...</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, we have books where the Antediluvians are central antagonists, and it feels like &quot;follow this plot road because of reasons&quot;, why my well connected Ventrue cant buy/steal a thermobaric weapon and hurt one or many of the antes? Why cant my strongly socially Tremere call his new mage friends and blast these monsters to oblivion? Well, because there is no meaningful way to measure any effect on them without stats.<br /> <br /> <br /> Stats are not just for killing, stats allow verisimilitude to the interactions &quot;<i>I try to sneak upon Augustus... Oh no, you cant he has HUMONGOUS Wits and detects everything</i>&quot;. The whole point of stats is to allow the representation of interactions, no stats = ST fiat, and that takes from the players choices.<br /> <br /> <br /> WW had products in which they relegated the PC to bystanders, but we are going to play as it should have been played: Derailing all the plots and saving the g*ddamn world, finishing one badly written adventure and dealing with one invincible NPC at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-26-2020, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T09:25:53-07:00","id":1383963,"title":"","content":"Great post! Gratz.<br /> <br /> Those stats are powerfull... Sadly we cannot even dream about making antes using v5 system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T09:50:52-07:00","id":1383969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1383959#post1383959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WW had products in which they relegated the PC to bystanders, but we are going to play as it should have been played: Derailing all the plots and saving the g*ddamn world, finishing one badly written adventure and dealing with one invincible NPC at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Duke Nukem. And not in a good way.<br /> <br /> Anyway, do like this: take the amount of xp you would give to your players per week/month/year/whatever. Then multiply it for at least 3000 years. Now use that enormous amount of point to create your sheet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T13:43:04-07:00","id":1384012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1383959#post1383959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree, we have books where the Antediluvians are central antagonists, and it feels like &quot;follow this plot road because of reasons&quot;, why my well connected Ventrue cant buy/steal a thermobaric weapon and hurt one or many of the antes? Why cant my strongly socially Tremere call his new mage friends and blast these monsters to oblivion? Well, because there is no meaningful way to measure any effect on them without stats.<br /> <br /> <br /> Stats are not just for killing, stats allow verisimilitude to the interactions &quot;<i>I try to sneak upon Augustus... Oh no, you cant he has HUMONGOUS Wits and detects everything</i>&quot;. The whole point of stats is to allow the representation of interactions, no stats = ST fiat, and that takes from the players choices.<br /> <br /> <br /> WW had products in which they relegated the PC to bystanders, but we are going to play as it should have been played: Derailing all the plots and saving the g*ddamn world, finishing one badly written adventure and dealing with one invincible NPC at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can of course play VtM as you see fit but saying it was meant to be played as yet another game of &quot;Kill the troll, steal the gold&quot; is blatantly false. Throughout its long history the WoD made a point of treating antediluvians, oracles, celestines, neverborn, etc as beings that were not to be killed by simply rolling dices. The whole system is called Storytelling System for a reason: it's the means to tell a story not just to roll dices and kill stuff with impunity.<br /> <br /> I've actually run a whole chronicle of ages and I can assure you a ST can have Antediluvians killed in the ST system without need of giving them stats. It's a matter of the players playing the game and doing the right choices at the right time, not just diablerize your way to infinite power and then roll a bucket of dices.<br /> <br /> As for your examples: can a Ventrue steal weapons capable to hurt an Ante? Going by what it took to kill Ravnos, no they can't (it was several supernatural factions working to stop Ravnos' rampage and the the most powerful supernatural faction of them all dropping a few nukes meant to dela with supernatural threats on him, followed by a concentrated ray of sunlight...). Can mages (and friends with the Tremere... XD) blast an Ante to oblivion? Mages capable of directly blasting an Ante to oblivion would be Oracles... and they don't work that way.<br /> <br /> You mistake stats with rules. Plot devices might not have stats (you go against them directly, you die) but they may have ways to defeat them. No one in the Lord of the Rings could even remotely come closer to defeat Sauron directly but there was no need to confront face to face, as he had a weakness (the one ring) that could be exploited to defeat him. In a chronicle about defeating the Antediluvians (or some of their progeny) the ST doesn't need to give the Antes stats. You face them and you die (as stated in more than one of the old WoD books...), UNLESS you play smart, do your job and find a way to make those blood gods actually defeatable. The way to do that is PLAYING THE CHRONICLE which is not synonimous with increasing your power until you can defeat a god in hand to hand combat.<br /> <br /> Lastly, nice try with the Augustus example. Unfortunately he was the one 3rd generation vampire that could actually be defeated with (relative) ease because his diablerie of Cappadocius failed and he had the potential power of a 3rd generation vampire (which does not mean having the power of an Antediluvian) but not the affective power level of one.<br /> <br /> Player agency doesn't mean doing whatever a player feels like he's entitled doing, nor expecting to be allowed to be given the means to kill gods. Plot devices don't need stats to be included into a chronicle and &quot;derailing the plots&quot; is usually not the best strategy for completing any kind of adventure unless the ST is someone who's willing to allow the players to do whatever they want and to get away with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:08:40-07:00","id":1384016,"title":"","content":"If it has stats players will want to kill it. That\u2019s why you don\u2019t stat them. I\u2019ve encountered a plethora of players who try to weasel through dominate and presence and get angry when they don\u2019t succeed. <br /> <br /> Devils advocate, many systems stat up top tier things and it\u2019s ok sometimes. <br /> <br /> The level 10 powers should be enough to stop players. <br /> <br /> You\u2019d have to homebrew some stuff. For example I wouldn\u2019t think tzimisce would be limited to 7 health levels. So you\u2019d have to figure in huge size merit and maybe add more merits that increase health levels. <br /> <br /> We\u2019re into stat them for fun, i would go 2000xp build. More combo disciplines. I personally never liked dice past 5. Exception to inhuman forms. <br /> <br /> I also consider do they have jack of all trades or anachronism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:23:44-07:00","id":1384018,"title":"","content":"I find nothing wrong with attempting to stat the Antes, its just a suggestion to use simplified rules.<br /> <br /> But for Giovanni I would have him not having access to level 10 disciplines, because its noted he had some sort of half Diablerie, he ate Cappy but Cappy set it up so he faked it and Gio never ate his soul.<br /> <br /> I would probably give the Eldest at least Kraina/Koldunic Sorcery at 9. And I like the idea he studied other shapeshifting powers so he learned Protean and Serpentis and Abombwe, and maybe a few unique powers at level 6. I would also probably have him have a lot of little things like Valeren all paths Three(get dat third eye), Quietus all paths 2. Maybe Necromancy 3 to represent he at least spent some time investigating things like the Underworld over the Eons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:25:28-07:00","id":1384019,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar19533_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"19533\" data-vbnamecard=\"19533\">Pnizzle</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24832_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24832\" data-vbnamecard=\"24832\">blailton</a><br /> <br /> Thanks for your answers, even if we disagree at least I got to see the &quot;why&quot; of other viewpoints.<br /> <br /> About the stats given, assuming the Gehenna book is valid as a data source, would it fit in V20 Chronicle with the scope expected of an antediluvian?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:30:36-07:00","id":1384021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384018#post1384018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find nothing wrong with attempting to stat the Antes, its just a suggestion to use simplified rules.<br /> <br /> But for Giovanni I would have him not having access to level 10 disciplines, because its noted he had some sort of half Diablerie, he ate Cappy but Cappy set it up so he faked it and Gio never ate his soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am using Gehenna, that states:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> he has no Level<br /> Ten Discipline to draw upon (he can perform only up to<br /> Level Five of his clan Discipline, Necromancy, as with<br /> all other Cainites) </div> </div> </div>But in Giovanni Chronicles he had Necromancy 9, the extra dot will do nothing because there are no powers per level, just rituals in V20 Necromancy. The paths are those that Giovanni know or that Cappadocians know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:32:47-07:00","id":1384022,"title":"","content":"Interesting<br /> <br /> I agree with the people who think you should never give Antediluvians stats because making them killable undermines the fundamental majesty and mystery of the WoD (it\u2019s like giving God 400 hit points...). My bff, OTOH, thinks that everything can be quantified and your PCs should be able to kill an Antediluvian if they play their cards right (after all, Gratiano came close to killing his clan founder\u2014or at least forcing her to discorporate and flee to the Abyss\u2014and he was just an upstart adventurer too...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:33:09-07:00","id":1384023,"title":"","content":"Well what I'm saying is he wouldn't have access to Necromancy 10 rituals until he finds and eats Cappy's soul and that is why he secretly is so desperate to find his ghost and eat it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:35:51-07:00","id":1384025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384023#post1384023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well what I'm saying is he wouldn't have access to Necromancy 10 rituals until he finds and eats Cappy's soul and that is why he secretly is so desperate to find his ghost and eat it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it, will recommend and apply adjustments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:36:43-07:00","id":1384026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384022#post1384022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting<br /> <br /> I agree with the people who think you should never give Antediluvians stats because making them killable undermines the fundamental majesty and mystery of the WoD (it\u2019s like giving God 400 hit points...). My bff, OTOH, thinks that everything can be quantified and your PCs should be able to kill an Antediluvian if they play their cards right (after all, Gratiano came close to killing his clan founder\u2014or at least forcing her to discorporate and flee to the Abyss\u2014and he was just an upstart adventurer too...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but not only about fighting, you want to roll over Subterfuge? Stealth? Diplomacy? Want to convince them to help you? You need others stats, again not just to fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> My point is, if you have to interact with them in any way, you need stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-26-2020, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:45:38-07:00","id":1384028,"title":"","content":"I guess...<br /> <br /> We usually just roleplay that stuff. Or at least give bonuses for good roleplaying.<br /> <br /> Is your name supposed to be Beaumanoir? There was a Templar grand master in Ivanhoe with that name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:46:24-07:00","id":1384029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384026#post1384026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but not only about fighting, you want to roll over Subterfuge? Stealth? Diplomacy? Want to convince them to help you? You need others stats, again not just to fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> My point is, if you have to interact with them in any way, you need stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely! Everytime I bring up interacting with Antes people say, nope you shouldn't do it because they will destroy lesser kindred. But people forgot Mithras played Chess with Haquim, Sutekh visits each of his Clan in a dream at embrace. Saulot has conversations with Sclav the Vozhd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:47:25-07:00","id":1384030,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> I love the chess game idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:54:38-07:00","id":1384033,"title":"","content":"Good to see some people are trying to stat the antes. I never liked the antes as unkillable blood gods. I am going to use a quote from the movie predator '' if it bleeds, it can be killed&quot; and as far as i am concerned they all bleed.<br /> <br /> But i have to say the stats the OP mentioned seem a bit weak for {Tzimisce}. He might be the most powerful of them all. Certainly top 3. He should have no stats below 7 and lots of 8's and 9's.<br /> <br /> But i would love to see people trying to stat all of them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 04-26-2020, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T15:09:02-07:00","id":1384038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384033#post1384033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good to see some people are trying to stat the antes. I never liked the antes as unkillable blood gods. I am going to use a quote from the movie predator '' if it bleeds, it can be killed&quot; and as far as i am concerned they all bleed.<br /> <br /> But i have to say the stats the OP mentioned seem a bit weak for {Tzimisce}. He might be the most powerful of them all. Certainly top 3. He should have no stats below 7 and lots of 8's and 9's.<br /> <br /> But i would love to see people trying to stat all of them</div> </div> </div> </div>Its debatable how powerful the Eldest is, but I wouldn't say it is definitely top three, it was killed by Samiel once and had to spend centuries reincarnating in the Dracon's Improvised Womb. The physical stats aren't listed, and the Eldest could likely have beyond 10 in physicals as it transcended the Human Frame, and we know it can turn into a giant dragon at the least and that would be a major stat boost. It also seemed to make use of minions a lot like Bogtyri.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T15:09:17-07:00","id":1384039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384029#post1384029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Precisely! Everytime I bring up interacting with Antes people say, nope you shouldn't do it because they will destroy lesser kindred. But people forgot Mithras played Chess with Haquim, Sutekh visits each of his Clan in a dream at embrace. Saulot has conversations with Sclav the Vozhd.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one really knows why Haqim visited Mithras, just that he did. Sutekh &quot;visiting&quot; all setites at embrace, if confirmed, could easily be just a powerful effect used by elders of the clan. And I fail to see why Saulot interacting with Sclav the Vozhd means anything in particular.<br /> <br /> And no, you don't need stats to interact with antediluvians. Let's say the chronicle requires your coterie to meet with one (not that I think this should happen with the players knowing who they are meeting unless it's endgame), you can just talk with it you don't need to affect it with powers and if you want to the ST can simply roll dices as he feels it's appropriate, because the scene with the antediluvian serves a plot point that is not about you outright fighting the ante.<br /> <br /> Again: you don't need stats to interact with plot devices, you need stats to confront them, which is a very different thing.<br /> <br /> @Eldagusto: Samiel killing the Tzimisce ante is just a story related in character by a Tzimisce as a legend of the clan. It's not a &quot;fact&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T15:19:52-07:00","id":1384042,"title":"","content":"I'd just assume they have all the clans disciplines and older combinations to a fairly high level. Not just their own. They may have missed out on some of the most recent bloodlines stuff, but they also ought to have scores to hundreds of dots in the long dead disciplines of bloodlines who are dust and forgotten aeons ago.<br /> <br /> There might be some surprises about whose clan disciplines are what. Haquim, Saulot, Ennoia, Troile, etc seems to have had childer with different clan discipline spread. Might be a bit random which line becomes the most numerous and sets the standard for what are the clan disciplines.<br /> <br /> I think there are some differences between the &quot;true&quot; Antediluvians though. Even a slight difference in interest and time spent on esoteric matters and powers is going to make a big difference if left to snowball for fifteen thousand years. And there were more than a slight difference in the Antediluvians attitudes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T16:00:04-07:00","id":1384047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384028#post1384028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is your name supposed to be Beaumanoir? There was a Templar grand master in Ivanhoe with that name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luc Beaumanoir, yes. It was inspired by that a long time ago, and I misswrote it, so here we are. Now it is quite unique on its own.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T16:09:55-07:00","id":1384050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384038#post1384038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its debatable how powerful the Eldest is, but I wouldn't say it is definitely top three, it was killed by Samiel once and had to spend centuries reincarnating in the Dracon's Improvised Womb. The physical stats aren't listed, and the Eldest could likely have beyond 10 in physicals as it transcended the Human Frame, and we know it can turn into a giant dragon at the least and that would be a major stat boost. It also seemed to make use of minions a lot like Bogtyri.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That proves my point. The Eldest is pretty much unkillable. You can destroy his body but he will still come back. The only way to kill him is to kill every vampire with tzimisce blood (that includes the tremere and every vampire that has tasted tzimisce blood). Which other ante can do that? He might be the only truly immortal out there. Not to mention he might be the only vampire with two beasts. He is a anomaly like no other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T16:13:30-07:00","id":1384051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384050#post1384050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That proves my point. The Eldest is pretty much unkillable. You can destroy his body but he will still come back. The only way to kill him is to kill every vampire with tzimisce blood (that includes the tremere and every vampire that has tasted tzimisce blood). Which other ante can do that? He might be the only truly immortal out there. Not to mention he might be the only vampire with two beasts. He is a anomaly like no other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but it seems Malkav is in a similar state. And I would imagine those with Soul magic or soul touch disciplines, Sorcery/Valeren/ect, could kill him permanently. And as described when he was Kamikaze smote by Samiel it was a major inconvenience that ate a lot of the Eldests Jyhad time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T16:53:16-07:00","id":1384056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384050#post1384050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That proves my point. The Eldest is pretty much unkillable. You can destroy his body but he will still come back. The only way to kill him is to kill every vampire with tzimisce blood (that includes the tremere and every vampire that has tasted tzimisce blood). Which other ante can do that? He might be the only truly immortal out there. Not to mention he might be the only vampire with two beasts. He is a anomaly like no other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he and Saulot are equivalent. If theres one vampire in golconda in the world that vampire is Saulot.This mean he could have disciplines over 10, maybe? Because the rules for golconda say a vampire whom achieved that could raise stats above the gen. cap. <br /> <br /> Just thinking.<br /> <br /> But in the gehenna scenario their fight end with both dying to the silly vodoo orchstred by saulot (where the pcs let be ate be him with that gonzo mc guffin and roll humanity)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T17:04:37-07:00","id":1384059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384038#post1384038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ,it was killed by Samiel once and had to spend centuries reincarnating in the Dracon's Improvised Womb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it was just like 9 months.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383952-v20-antediluvians-peach?p=1384039#post1384039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> @Eldagusto: Samiel killing the Tzimisce ante is just a story related in character by a Tzimisce as a legend of the clan. It's not a &quot;fact&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it is confirmed by no one less than the Dracon himself. <br /> Well, maybe it is not confirmed that it was Samiel, sure, but that he died... yes, that's canon, as we are told by the only vampire who could actually say &quot;yes it happened&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Clan Novel Tzimisce Dark Ages<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are those who say that I am my sire\u2019s firstchosen and favorite. They are only partially correct. The pride of place for the first-chosen rightfully belongs an elder brother whose name is now all but forgotten and whose line has so dwindled that if it contains a dozen childer, I would be surprised, indeed. But favorite? Yes, I was that. I say it, and claim the truth of it, without pride and without pleasure. My sire loves me, not as a man loves his lover, but as a father loves his son. You cannot imagine how terrifying that is, how heavy a weight it hangs upon my shoulders, to know that in me resides the sum of my sire\u2019s remaining humanity, the remnants of his ability to feel and comprehend human emotion, the womb of his rebirth as a thing only barely human any longer.<b> It is almost true, that he cannot die</b>. So long as one of his blood exists, he exists. So long as the world does not fall to ash, he may make himself whole again.<b> It happened once. His flesh perished, but his essence lived on, lived on and found purchase within me to remake itself. I felt both things, almost at once\u2014the shock of his death, rippling through the blood in my veins, and the second, greater shock of his life, quickening within the blood that he had given me, within my very flesh</b>. I felt him reshape me to host himself, building a nest within me of blood and soft tissue, to cradle a tiny seed of recovering consciousness. I felt him grow, slowly, as he drew the scattered pieces of himself, the fragments of his identity, back together again, growing stronger and more coherent as the weeks stretched into months. <b>Nine months, of course, nine the number it takes to create miracles of new life</b>. My belly swelled with him and within myself, I felt him move, I felt him caress me from within, lovingly, trusting me in his vulnerability as he trusted no one and nothing else, even his bogatyr witch-warriors. I knew how a woman must feel as her babe grew beneath her heart, and it nearly drove me mad to discover that same depth of love within myself for my sire, whose soul I carried within me, whose blood and flesh were as much my own as his. He birthed himself on a moonless night, as my body contorted with the demands he made on it, yielding flesh and blood as he required. I know there was pain, but the pain is not the most intense memory I have of that night. Rather, it was laying there afterwards, panting and as exhausted as any woman who had birthed her first child, with him laying on my hollowed-out belly, small and red and wrinkled. He mewled, hungrily, as any infant would, and I took him in my arms, gave him suck from my own throat\u2014and when I looked into his eyes, I saw that his effort to recreate himself had failed. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T17:53:04-07:00","id":1384063,"title":"","content":"As for statting Ante... it can be done...but it is useless for the reasons that have been explained...gods...stats...unkillable...plot device...yada yada yada<br /> <br /> <br /> That said...if someone wants to stats the unstattable, he should look at how the unstattable as been statted before.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is Nergal sheet, it's the closest thing you will ever had to an Antediluvian sheet (a 4th gen vampire from the Second City that was elevated by demonic powers...close enough)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Huitzilopochtli</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <b>clan</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Baali\" target=\"_blank\">Baali</a></span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <b>sire</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ashur_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">Ashur</a></span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <b>nature</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Architect</span><br /> </span><